Track 3: Corona Cantante
- Story & Context: Legend tells of the Corona Cantante, the "Singing Crown" of pure plasma that briefly forms around the eclipsed sun, and how its silent, resonating frequency is what draws the Lunáticos to their sacred dance. During the last total eclipse, a collective shudder ran through the crowd as a single, sustained, impossibly low tone vibrated through the earth itself, causing small objects to hum and a flock of birds to fly in dizzying, erratic circles. "The sun's hidden song makes our bones hum," murmured a priestess, her eyes fixed on the impossible halo.
